---
import LegalArticle from "@components/common/LegalArticle.astro"
import { site } from "@data/site"
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import { waLink } from "@lib/whatsapp"

// Mesmo conteúdo de /privacidade/, em inglês. Manter os dois em sincronia.
const analytics = Boolean(site.umamiWebsiteId)
const ads = Boolean(site.googleAds.tagId)
const controller = site.legalName
  ? `${site.name} (${site.legalName})`
  : site.name
const dataRequest = waLink(
  "Hi! I have a request about my personal data (LGPD).",
)
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  routeKey="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy | Hello World Estúdio"
  description="How the Hello World Estúdio website handles personal data: WhatsApp contact, cookieless usage metrics and your rights under Brazil's LGPD."
>
  <LegalArticle title="Privacy Policy" updated="Last updated: October 7, 2026">
    <p>
      This policy explains, in plain language, what personal data this website
      processes, why, for how long and how you can exercise your rights under
      Brazil's General Data Protection Law (Law No. 13,709/2018, the LGPD).
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>{controller}</strong>, Brazilian company registration (CNPJ){" "}
      {site.cnpj}, is a software studio from{" "}
      {`${site.address.locality} (${site.address.region})`}, Brazil, that works
      fully online, and is the controller of the personal data processed through
      this website.
    </p>

    <h2>Data subject channel and DPO</h2>
    <p>
      As a small-sized processing agent, we are exempt from appointing a data
      protection officer (ANPD Resolution CD/ANPD No. 2/2022). Even so, any
      question or request about your data is handled directly by{" "}
      {site.founder.name}, founder, on WhatsApp at{" "}
      <a href={dataRequest} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        {site.whatsapp.display}
      </a>{" "}
      or by email at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What data we process and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>WhatsApp or email contact.</strong> When you reach out, we
        receive the data you choose to send, such as your name, phone number and
        a description of your project. We use it to reply, prepare proposals
        and, if we work together, deliver the service. Legal basis:
        pre-contractual steps and performance of a contract (LGPD, art. 7, V).
        WhatsApp is a Meta service, which processes conversation data under its
        own privacy policy.
      </li>
      {analytics ? (
        <li>
          <strong>Usage metrics.</strong> We use Umami, a metrics tool that does
          not use cookies or identify you individually. It records aggregated
          data such as pages visited, referrer, device type and clicks on
          contact buttons, so we can understand what works on the website. Legal
          basis: legitimate interest (LGPD, art. 7, IX).
        </li>
      ) : (
        <li>
          <strong>Usage metrics.</strong> This website does not use analytics or
          visitor tracking tools.
        </li>
      )}
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting.</strong> The website is hosted on Cloudflare, which
        processes technical request data (such as IP address and browser) to
        deliver pages and protect the site against attacks. Legal basis:
        legitimate interest (LGPD, art. 7, IX).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The website has no forms or sign-up, the only login area is the blog panel
      described above, and we never ask for sensitive data (health, religion,
      biometrics, etc.). We also do not make automated decisions about you based
      on your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Blog panel (for clients who subscribe to the blog)</h2>
    <p>
      Clients who subscribe to a blog plan write and publish articles through a
      panel at <strong>cms.helloworldestudio.com.br</strong>. In it, we process:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email and name (optional)</strong> of the people who use the
        panel, registered by the studio, to identify who signs in and to send
        notices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>6-digit login code</strong>, sent by email. We store only its
        hash, it is valid for 10 minutes and is removed from the database after
        it expires.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>IP address</strong>, to limit login attempts (security) and for
        the anti-bot check. It is stored with the login code and deleted with
        it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Activity log</strong> (published, unpublished, deleted an
        article, changed details, exported a copy), linked to the email of the
        person who acted, for security and to give the studio and the client a
        history.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Uploaded articles and images</strong>, to publish the client's
        blog. The content belongs to the client.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Payment record</strong> (date, period and agreed amount), to
        calculate the plan's due date. Payment happens outside the system, over
        WhatsApp: the panel receives no card or bank account data.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Legal basis: contract performance (art. 7, V, LGPD) and, for the IP
      address and activity log, legitimate interest in security (art. 7, IX). We
      are the controller of login and billing data of the people who use the
      panel. The content of the articles, and data about people the client
      mentions in them, is the client's responsibility (controller), and we act
      as processor. Clients in regulated fields, such as law, are responsible
      for the professional secrecy of what they publish.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Who reads the blog:</strong> the panel installs no cookies or
      trackers on the client's website and does not collect visitor data. The
      blog is generated as static pages. Access statistics, if any, come from
      the tools declared in that website's own policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      The panel uses the providers <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (hosting of the
      panel and API, database, image storage and anti-bot check at login) and{" "}
      <strong>Resend</strong> (sending the login code, welcome and due-date
      emails).
    </p>

    <h2>Data in client projects</h2>
    <p>
      When we build a system for your company, we may access data about your
      customers or employees. In those cases your company is the controller and
      we act as the processor: we handle that data only to deliver the project,
      following your instructions and the contract, and never use it for any
      other purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    {ads ? (
      <p>
        This website uses the Google Ads tag only to measure whether one of our
        ads led to a WhatsApp contact. Google may set cookies in your browser
        when you arrive from an ad. We do not use this data for remarketing or
        profiling. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings and
        manage ads at{" "}
        <a
          href="https://adssettings.google.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          adssettings.google.com
          <span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
        . Cloudflare may also set strictly necessary cookies for security.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies, so it shows
        no consent banner. Cloudflare may set strictly necessary cookies for
        security.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      The blog panel (<strong>cms.helloworldestudio.com.br</strong>) uses a
      single cookie, <code>hwcms_session</code>, strictly necessary to keep you
      signed in: without it there is no login. It only exists after login, lasts
      30 days, is <code>HttpOnly</code>, <code>Secure</code> and{" "}
      <code>SameSite=Lax</code>, does not track you or serve ads, and therefore
      needs no consent. The panel uses no analytics or advertising cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell or share your data for marketing purposes. It only goes
      through the providers listed above, as far as each service requires, or to
      authorities when required by law or court order.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Some of these providers (Cloudflare, Resend and Meta
      {analytics && ", as well as Umami"}
      {ads && ", as well as Google"}) may process data on servers outside
      Brazil. These transfers follow article 33 of the LGPD and rely on the
      contractual data protection safeguards each provider offers.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Conversations that did not become a project:</strong> up to 2
        years after the last contact, so we can pick up where we left off if you
        come back. After that, we delete them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Clients:</strong> for the length of the contract and, after it,
        for the period required by legal and tax obligations (usually 5 years).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Blog panel:</strong> login and billing data are kept while the
        plan is active and during the 30 days after it expires, when the panel
        stays open only to download a copy of the articles and images. After
        that, only for the period required by law or contract. Removing a person
        from the panel disables their access immediately, and the activity log
        is kept as history.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical access data:</strong> for each provider's retention
        period, with no link to your identity.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you ask for deletion before that, we delete everything we are not
      legally required to keep.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The website only works over an encrypted connection (HTTPS) and sends
      security headers on every page. Access to conversations and client data is
      limited to the people working on the project, on accounts protected by
      two-factor authentication. If a security incident could put you at risk,
      we will notify you and the ANPD, as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the LGPD (art. 18), you may request at any time, free of charge:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>confirmation that we process your data, and access to it;</li>
      <li>correction of incomplete, inaccurate or outdated data;</li>
      <li>
        anonymization, blocking or deletion of unnecessary data or data
        processed in breach of the law;
      </li>
      <li>
        portability of your data to another provider (blog clients download a
        copy of their articles and images, as a ZIP, from the panel itself);
      </li>
      <li>information about who we share your data with;</li>
      <li>
        objection to processing based on legitimate interest, and withdrawal of
        consent where applicable.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Just message us on WhatsApp at{" "}
      <a href={dataRequest} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        {site.whatsapp.display}
      </a>{" "}
      or by email at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We may
      ask you to confirm your identity first, to protect your data, and we reply
      within 15 days. If you are not satisfied, you may also file a complaint
      with Brazil's{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.gov.br/anpd/pt-br"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        National Data Protection Authority (ANPD)
        <span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Children and teenagers</h2>
    <p>
      This website and our services are aimed at businesses and adults. We do
      not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages link to third-party websites (such as LinkedIn and WhatsApp).
      Once you click, that website's privacy policy applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated when the website or the law changes. The date
      at the top shows the current version.
    </p>
  </LegalArticle>
</BaseLayout>
